.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_character_tables \- set character tables
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_set_character_tables\fP\f(CR(pcre2_compile_context *\fP\f(CIccontext\fP\f(CR,
                               const uint8_t *\fP\f(CItables\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function sets a pointer to custom character tables within a compile
context. The second argument must point to a set of PCRE2 character tables or
be \f(CBNULL\fP to request the default tables. The result is always zero. Character
tables can be created by calling \f(CBpcre2_maketables()\fP or by running the
\f(CRpcre2_dftables\fP maintenance command in binary mode (see the
\f(CRpcre2build\fP
documentation).
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.